{"title":"Power Mean Inequality","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>Power Mean Inequality</b> is a generalized form of the multi-variable <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic_Mean-Geometric_Mean\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Arithmetic Mean-Geometric Mean\">Arithmetic Mean-Geometric Mean</a> Inequality.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Inequality\">Inequality</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Power_Mean_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Inequality\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positive real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positive real weights <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/5/535b2bfbb0a587e261a0d0af9b7b53e42629b14d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> with sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e5308b0631e6ae2b13af6ce5582f91dbe31631.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^n w_i=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"79\" height=\"48\" />, the power mean with exponent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6cca0fe10c8b6f4afe50dbf6fb64a88d8f8a1abe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t\\in\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />, is defined by\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/8/e883aefc639005872d192501d4e117a7c89ef42d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[M(t)= \\begin{cases} \\prod_{i=1}^n a_i^{w_i} &amp;\\text{if } t=0 \\\\ \\left(\\sum_{i=1}^n w_ia_i^t \\right)^{\\frac{1}{t}} &amp;\\text{otherwise} \\end{cases}.\\]\" width=\"274\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/4/554d37556f3c0a95d4a168f264db6fb47d48f3ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M(0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"20\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AM-GM_Inequality#Weighted_AM-GM_Inequality\" title=\"AM-GM Inequality\">weighted geometric mean</a>.)\n</p><p>The Power Mean Inequality states that for all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f2f57887b2e2f63a617b6a4b7a7d466c26c4342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb72004e1c6c7b0782bbf2c7e40dcaad72993c4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b3548c7e02c7ddb1ff4f2e94c468013ccbb759f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M(k_1)\\ge M(k_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b34ff333a3aa5880054f310d5e66143a8a3ff37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1&gt;k_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />. In particular, for nonzero <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f2f57887b2e2f63a617b6a4b7a7d466c26c4342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb72004e1c6c7b0782bbf2c7e40dcaad72993c4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, and equal weights (i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/0/1c094db8e37d9e44a5b3bf9c4757d69789df61ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_i=1/n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />), if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b34ff333a3aa5880054f310d5e66143a8a3ff37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1&gt;k_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />, then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/2717382a9f9044a15ad493c7d136ec5b3e1099c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left( \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^n a_{i}^{k_1} \\right)^{\\frac{1}{k_1}}  \\ge \\left( \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^n a_{i}^{k_2} \\right)^{\\frac{1}{k_2}}.\\]\" width=\"259\" height=\"59\" /> \n</p><p>Considering the limiting behavior, we also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/d/ead2effca3ba1d85c6912aebe436752cb14ca1db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{t\\rightarrow +\\infty} M(t)=\\max\\{a_i\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"175\" height=\"26\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30b0305ad90a547a111879bf65de6fbfce931e31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{t\\rightarrow -\\infty} M(t)=\\min\\{a_i\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"172\" height=\"25\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c2af58119ea2625d3de34d735d9c22290ac99c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{t\\rightarrow 0} M(t)= M(0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"134\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>The Power Mean Inequality follows from <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Jensen%27s_Inequality\" title=\"Jensen&#39;s Inequality\">Jensen's Inequality</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Power_Mean_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We prove by cases:\n</p><p>1. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/0/390eed088ba809fad97b3c496653458763ef80c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M(t)\\ge M(0)\\ge M(-t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"184\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/2/a027a3809fbe4d5dc820151b567718df14a4e85e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>2. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b3548c7e02c7ddb1ff4f2e94c468013ccbb759f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M(k_1)\\ge M(k_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/8/a28560c7adbf559a15a9b00bb7db737bad45ed1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1 \\ge k_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/6/126519d17eced84761b15752305ab5f009b9eac4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1k_2&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Case 1:\n</p><p>Note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/f/60f6c9a4f3cbc5ab159bc96045379d0d3d582691.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} &amp;&amp; \\left(\\sum_{i=1}^n w_ia_i^{t} \\right)^{\\frac{1}{t}} &amp;\\ge \\prod_{i=1}^n a_i^{w_i} \\\\ \\Longleftarrow &amp;&amp; \\frac{1}{t} \\ln\\left( \\sum_{i=1}^n w_i a_i^{t} \\right) &amp;\\ge \\sum_{i=1}^n w_i \\ln{a_i} &amp;&amp; \\text{as } e^x \\text{ is increasing} \\\\ \\Longleftarrow &amp;&amp; \\ln\\left( \\sum_{i=1}^n w_i a_i^{t} \\right) &amp;\\ge \\sum_{i=1}^n w_i \\ln{a_i^t} &amp;&amp; \\text{as } t&gt;0 \\end{align*}\" width=\"436\" height=\"179\" />\nAs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/0/d507b554c198a284b1e1974447663e8ab8b62e6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ln(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is concave, by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Jensen%27s_Inequality\" title=\"Jensen&#39;s Inequality\">Jensen's Inequality</a>, the last inequality is true, proving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/2/422d5ece05af8bf791f627a8f1abafdee2158355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M(t)\\ge M(0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" />. By replacing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/8/ca8dc0e291b5b158e7b9d4cbb2d7aee87c77904c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-t$\" width=\"20\" height=\"11\" />, the last inequality implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/8/d28b2722849eb86b31902c1e7169558ad69151c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M(0)\\ge M(-t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" /> as the inequality signs are flipped after multiplication by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/4/d641b337228712a5a23a399f69026d8b0ed2a059.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{1}{t}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"25\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nCase 2:\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27a160281e9088165c59b6f89eb638051e35709.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1\\ge k_2&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/2/122f2a0fd1894df6d2635d38c249fbc63caf2dc5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align} &amp;&amp; \\left(\\sum_{i=1}^n w_ia_i^{k_1} \\right)^{\\frac{1}{k_1}} &amp;\\ge \\left(\\sum_{i=1}^n w_ia_i^{k_2} \\right)^{\\frac{1}{k_2}} \\nonumber \\\\ \\Longleftarrow &amp;&amp; \\left(\\sum_{i=1}^n w_ia_i^{k_1} \\right)^{\\frac{k_2}{k_1}} &amp;\\ge \\sum_{i=1}^n w_ia_i^{k_2} \\label{eq} \\end{align}\" width=\"413\" height=\"127\" />\nAs the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08cff4abe60b632e2cecd15f9f5a475c9bb6102b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x^{\\frac{k_2}{k_1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"24\" /> is concave for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/cae4fd68f44ac9b909f8d91f9d498de5759bb45b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Jensen%27s_Inequality\" title=\"Jensen&#39;s Inequality\">Jensen's Inequality</a>,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/7/7a76d5618728cd8487eeea3c7d678757c65a2cdd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^n w_i a_i^{k_1} \\right)^{\\frac{k_2}{k_1}} = f\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^n w_i a_i^{k_1} \\right) \\geq \\sum_{i=1}^n w_i f\\left(a_i^{k_1}\\right) =\\sum_{i=1}^n w_i a_{i}^{k_2}\\]\" width=\"469\" height=\"60\" />\nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/7/b0707f04216e3ac6ce2c21c2d90135d48a087d28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&gt;k_1\\ge k_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> becomes convex as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/8/55876fe2dad5fc0eca7d4e67256afafbbcd69992.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|k_1|\\le |k_2|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />, so the inequality sign when applying Jensen's Inequality is flipped. Thus, the inequality sign in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> is flipped, but as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/978a626221eee093d338bd8e14b03532184b1ed8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_2&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/3/3d303a21a6ae6a8aace2d7b24418c2ecef91f051.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^\\frac{1}{k_2}$\" width=\"25\" height=\"19\" /> is a decreasing function, the inequality sign is flipped again after applying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/1/3f1a709d45888b5ff354839e88b2f7997fd9de7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{\\frac{1}{k_2}}$\" width=\"25\" height=\"19\" />, resulting in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b3548c7e02c7ddb1ff4f2e94c468013ccbb759f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M(k_1)\\ge M(k_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" /> as desired.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017220511\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.027 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 189/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9314/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:1611:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017220511 and revision id 225600. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}